# omarchy-settings ships the same files on every architecture when its source
# has this file: the recipe stops leaving the x86_64 memory stack (swap on
# zram, zswap off, the reclaim sysctls, systemd-oomd's slice policy, USB
# autosuspend) and the Thunderbolt module out of the aarch64 package.
#
# The N1x branch runs only on the NVIDIA N1x laptops, which need that stack as
# much as x86_64 does: without it they boot with no swap at all while
# systemd-oomd watches a pressure policy nobody configured. The HOOKS line in
# etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/omarchy_hooks.conf carries its own Apple Silicon guard,
# as the recipe requires of a source that ships it unwrapped.
#
# omacom/omarchy#13362 brings this file upstream, with the runtime checks Apple
# Silicon needs for each of these files; take its version when this branch
# moves onto it.
